import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Playing around with CODEPEN.io" description="Playing around with CODEPEN.io - readysaltedcode story">
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/stories">Stories</a>
      </nav>
      <h1>Playing around with CODEPEN.io</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="story-content">
    <div class="container">
      <p>CodePen is a playground for the front end side of the web. It's all about inspiration, education, and sharing.</p>
      <p>Need to build a reduced test case to demonstrate and figure out a bug? CodePen is great for that. Want to show off your latest creation and get feedback from your peers? CodePen is great for that. Want to find example of a particular design pattern for you project? CodePen is great for that. I am already having fun and only signed up about 20mins ago.</p>
      <p>As my dance project has lots of data visulisation using javascript, I thought that i would play around with an online tool - not my best code so be kind.</p>
      <p><object width="”650″" height="”600″" classid="clsid:d27cdb6e-ae6d-11cf-96b8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0"><param name="src" value="http://codepen.io/readysaltedcode/pen/xryDu" /><embed width="”650″" height="”600″" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" src="https://codepen.io/readysaltedcode/pen/xryDu" /></object></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }
  .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: #ccc; }
  .page-header h1 { color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
